# sirius: SystemOS union mount verified (2026-10-28 14:50 capture)
#
# Kernel c9f51f3b9278c00b01d7e3503788682b8643ecfdc743268fa7450fc61dcac37d, the build with
# sirius-systemos-union.patch; payload-full.img sha256 ddac80bd...; boot args include
# sirius_systemos_union=1. Captured from /dev/ttyACM0 while the phone booted after
# `fastboot flash vendor payload-full.img` (14:07) and `fastboot erase misc; fastboot reboot`.
#
# What it shows: before the union the mount table is the OS volume (disk2s1) plus /dev; the
# SystemOS volume is found by its UUID (8846FE78-...), mounted as /dev/disk4s1 with
# MNT_RDONLY|MNT_UNION over "/", and the dyld cache lookups go from ENOENT to 0. launchd then
# execs and issues the same 24 syscalls; the union is no longer the stop.
#
# The raw 7.8 MB capture is .scratch/console-union-20261028-1450.log (the eMMC per-read trace
# dominates it, and the ring replays on each host byte); this is the first boot replay, trimmed
# to the storage, union, exec, syscall and pad-state lines.
#
